King Meran threw the book closed, tossed it to the ground, and slouched in his throne, numbed with boredom to the core of his bones. He looked around the room at the small groups of his realm\'92s inhabitants he had chosen to employ as they skulked in the corners. The ones he gave sanctuary to in return for their help in stewarding the kingdom, were always kept nearby, a quick snap of his fingers away.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\ql\sl276\slmult1{\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\aspalpha\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\cf0\kerning0\hich\af2\langfe2052\dbch\af2\afs24\lang1081\loch\f3\fs22\lang4105\sl100\slmult0\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi720{\cf1\hich\af8\dbch\af8\rtlch \ltrch\loch\fs24\loch\f6
Whether it was for mundane tasks such as having someone draw a portrait of him while he watched the sun set and the moon rise through a window in the drawing room, or if he just needed a quick errand done, such as the penning of letters to someone in the neighbouring three kingdoms; Something of import was almost always on his mind, but the thought currently running rampant inside his brain had nothing to do with the plethora of elves, goblins, changelings, bogeys, redcaps, imps. These and numerous other fae were definitely }{\cf1\i\hich\af8\dbch\af8\ai\rtlch \ltrch\loch\fs24\loch\f6
not}{\cf1\hich\af8\dbch\af8\rtlch \ltrch\loch\fs24\loch\f6
