Of }{\cf1\i\hich\af8\dbch\af8\ai\rtlch \ltrch\loch\fs24\loch\f6
course}{\cf1\rtlch \ltrch\loch
 }{\cf1\hich\af8\dbch\af8\rtlch \ltrch\loch\fs24\loch\f6
you'd say that about me.\'94 Marie scoffed and rolled her eyes. I elbowed her in the ribs and then squeezed her shoulder as hard as I could. She hissed in pain and finally clamped her mouth closed. I hoped she\'92d keep it shut.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\ql\sl276\slmult1{\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\aspalpha\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\cf0\kerning0\hich\af2\langfe2052\dbch\af2\afs24\lang1081\loch\f3\fs22\lang4105\sl100\slmult0\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi720{\cf1\rtlch \ltrch
\'93}{\cf1\hich\af8\dbch\af8\rtlch \ltrch\loch\fs24\loch\f6
You two would do well to listen to her.\'94 The imp said, flicking its gaze between Marie and Toni, pointing its thin, bony index finger at me. \'93She seems wise beyond her years.\'94 He dropped his finger, tightening the grip he had on the handle of his pitchfork.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\ql\sl276\slmult1{\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\aspalpha\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\cf0\kerning0\hich\af2\langfe2052\dbch\af2\afs24\lang1081\loch\f3\fs22\lang4105\sl100\slmult0\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi720{\cf1\rtlch \ltrch
\'93}{\cf1\hich\af8\dbch\af8\rtlch \ltrch\loch\fs24\loch\f6
Tell me, human. What is your name?\'94 He asked. As he spoke his eyes swept over us all, eventually resting on me as he finished speaking, an impassive expression on his face. I could tell he was sizing us up and trying to decipher our motives just as much as Toni and I were.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\ql\sl276\slmult1{\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\aspalpha\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\cf0\kerning0\hich\af2\langfe2052\dbch\af2\afs24\lang1081\loch\f3\fs22\lang4105\sl100\slmult0\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi720{\cf1\rtlch \ltrch
\'93}{\cf1\hich\af8\dbch\af8\rtlch \ltrch\loch\fs24\loch\f6
My name is Zoey Cre.\'94 I responded. An almost imperceptible twitch of his brow ridge caused it to rise ever so slightly at my answer, but it quickly came back down.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\ql\sl276\slmult1{\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\aspalpha\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\cf0\kerning0\hich\af2\langfe2052\dbch\af2\afs24\lang1081\loch\f3\fs22\lang4105\sl100\slmult0\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi720{\cf1\i\hich\af8\dbch\af8\ai\rtlch \ltrch\loch\fs24\loch\f6
Does he}{\cf1\hich\af8\dbch\af8\rtlch \ltrch\loch\fs24\loch\f6
 }{\cf1\i\hich\af8\dbch\af8\ai\rtlch \ltrch\loch\fs24\loch\f6
recognize my name? }{\cf1\hich\af8\dbch\af8\rtlch \ltrch\loch\fs24\loch\f6
Seeing as we had just met, I couldn't fathom how that could be possible. I decided then that I had no reason to trust him any further than I could throw him. Despite his short stature and my telekinetic ability, I doubted that was anything more than a few feet at most. My gaze shifted over to his pitchfork. It was small, but he held it as if he knew exactly how to use it. I probably didn\'92t stand a chance of getting anywhere near him and attempting to disarm him, especially with only a measly pocket knife and a superpower that I didn't have a handle on at my disposal.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\ql\sl276\slmult1{\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\aspalpha\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\cf0\kerning0\hich\af2\langfe2052\dbch\af2\afs24\lang1081\loch\f3\fs22\lang4105\sl100\slmult0\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi720{\cf1\rtlch \ltrch
\'93}{\cf1\hich\af8\dbch\af8\rtlch \ltrch\loch\fs24\loch\f6
I\'92m pretty sure I\'92m not entirely human anymore either. As you can see, I have what I\'92m fairly certain are elvish ears.\'94 I turned my head to the side and pointed my free hand at my ear to show him. His eyes narrowed and I could have sworn I heard his heartbeat slow. Then again, I wasn\'92t entirely sure if it was his heart I was hearing, one of my friend\'92s, or some other unknown fourth person.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\ql\sl276\slmult1{\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\aspalpha\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\cf0\kerning0\hich\af2\langfe2052\dbch\af2\afs24\lang1081\loch\f3\fs22\lang4105\sl100\slmult0\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi720{\cf1\i\hich\af8\dbch\af8\ai\rtlch \ltrch\loch\fs24\loch\f6
Gods, I hope no one else is nearby!}
\par \pard\plain \s0\ql\sl276\slmult1{\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\aspalpha\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\cf0\kerning0\hich\af2\langfe2052\dbch\af2\afs24\lang1081\loch\f3\fs22\lang4105\sl100\slmult0\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi720{\cf1\rtlch \ltrch
\'93}{\cf1\hich\af8\dbch\af8\rtlch \ltrch\loch\fs24\loch\f6
To answer your question though, I\'92m 20. One second, my friends and I were on a camping trip by ourselves and the next we were here, in this forest, without most of our provisions.\'94 I chose not to mention my bracelet, as I still wasn\'92t sure he could be trusted. }{\cf1\rtlch \ltrch\loch
\'93}{\cf1\hich\af8\dbch\af8\rtlch \ltrch\loch\fs24\loch\f6
Now please. Could you tell us where we are? It feels different here. Does this place have a proper name? Speaking of names, what\'92s yours?\'94 I asked him some of the most pertinent questions I had. Most important to me was where we were. I was hoping that it wouldn\'92t take us too long to get back to our campsite. }{\cf1\i\hich\af8\dbch\af8\ai\rtlch \ltrch\loch\fs24\loch\f6
Depending on our location and proximity to it... If we\'92re far away, it could take us days! Or even worse, weeks! We don\'92t have the provisions needed for a trip like that! Oh, shit! That reminds me... What about all our food??}
\par \pard\plain \s0\ql\sl276\slmult1{\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\aspalpha\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\cf0\kerning0\hich\af2\langfe2052\dbch\af2\afs24\lang1081\loch\f3\fs22\lang4105\sl100\slmult0\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi720{\cf1\hich\af8\dbch\af8\rtlch \ltrch\loch\fs24\loch\f6
He answered my questions in reverse order. \'93Firstly, My name is Hortic. Secondly, we are standing in the Tipua Forest, near the eastern border of the Kingdom of Korvus. It is ruled by his highness, King Meran. I assume that you\'92re from the Other Side, otherwise I'd expect you'd know all this. Am I correct?\'94 He gave me a look that told me to think carefully before I answered.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\ql\sl276\slmult1{\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\aspalpha\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\cf0\kerning0\hich\af2\langfe2052\dbch\af2\afs24\lang1081\loch\f3\fs22\lang4105\sl100\slmult0\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi720{\cf1\hich\af8\dbch\af8\rtlch \ltrch\loch\fs24\loch\f6
Assuming what he was telling me was the truth, I surmised that the Other Side referred to our home and nodded.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\ql\sl276\slmult1{\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\aspalpha\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\cf0\kerning0\hich\af2\langfe2052\dbch\af2\afs24\lang1081\loch\f3\fs22\lang4105\sl100\slmult0\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi720{\cf1\rtlch \ltrch
\'93}{\cf1\hich\af8\dbch\af8\rtlch \ltrch\loch\fs24\loch\f6
I see. You must be lost then.\'94 He said, looking up his nose snootily, like he couldn't be bothered to assist us in any way. \'93Regardless, I am not a tour guide nor do I have time to babysit some snot-nosed punk and her know-it-all little friend.\'94 He eyed Marie with a look of derision and then gazed up at me. \'93Now then, I'm getting bored of this and do not want to incur the king's wrath if I am late. Good day, madame!\'94 Clearly annoyed, he huffed, turned, and walked past me, putting his pitchfork into a small hilt on his waist belt that I hadn\'92t noticed before.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\ql\sl276\slmult1{\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\aspalpha\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\cf0\kerning0\hich\af2\langfe2052\dbch\af2\afs24\lang1081\loch\f3\fs22\lang4105\sl100\slmult0\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi720{\cf1\i\hich\af8\dbch\af8\ai\rtlch \ltrch\loch\fs24\loch\f6
Was that there earlier? Why didn't I notice it before? Had it been magickally hidden from view?}
\par \pard\plain \s0\ql\sl276\slmult1{\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\aspalpha\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\cf0\kerning0\hich\af2\langfe2052\dbch\af2\afs24\lang1081\loch\f3\fs22\lang4105\sl100\slmult0\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi720{\cf1\rtlch \ltrch
\'93}{\cf1\hich\af8\dbch\af8\rtlch \ltrch\loch\fs24\loch\f6
Wait! How did we get here?! Can you help us get back to our campground?\'94 Marie frantically shouted. Having finally managed to escape my grip, she pushed her way up off the log before I could grab her, broke into a jog and followed Hortic.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\ql\sl276\slmult1{\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\aspalpha\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\cf0\kerning0\hich\af2\langfe2052\dbch\af2\afs24\lang1081\loch\f3\fs22\lang4105\sl100\slmult0\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi720{\cf1\rtlch \ltrch
\'93}{\cf1\hich\af8\dbch\af8\rtlch \ltrch\loch\fs24\loch\f6
Shit, Marie! What are you doing? Wait!\'94 I yelled, throwing my hands up in the air in frustration, more at myself for not making sure she was securely held down than at the fact that she was chasing after a total stranger. After making sure my Camelbak still had the granola bars and water bottles I had packed, I grabbed Toni\'92s hand and pulled her up.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\ql\sl276\slmult1{\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\aspalpha\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\cf0\kerning0\hich\af2\langfe2052\dbch\af2\afs24\lang1081\loch\f3\fs22\lang4105\sl100\slmult0\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi720{\cf1\rtlch \ltrch
\'93}{\cf1\hich\af8\dbch\af8\rtlch \ltrch\loch\fs24\loch\f6
Come on, Toni! We both know Marie won\'92t survive long without us!\'94 Raising one brow at me sceptically, she begrudgingly nodded and we went after Marie.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\ql\sl276\slmult1{\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\aspalpha\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\cf0\kerning0\hich\af2\langfe2052\dbch\af2\afs24\lang1081\loch\f3\fs22\lang4105\sl100\slmult0\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi720{\cf1\hich\af8\dbch\af8\rtlch \ltrch\loch\fs24\loch\f6
Hearing us trailing him, Hortic stopped for a moment and turned around. \'93You humans are wicked, vile and wildly ill-tempered things.\'94 He rolled his eyes at Marie and only continued speaking after he made sure we all were paying close attention and hanging on to his every word.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\ql\sl276\slmult1{\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\aspalpha\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\cf0\kerning0\hich\af2\langfe2052\dbch\af2\afs24\lang1081\loch\f3\fs22\lang4105\sl100\slmult0\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi720{\cf1\rtlch \ltrch
\'93}{\cf1\hich\af8\dbch\af8\rtlch \ltrch\loch\fs24\loch\f6
Verily, I do believe your harebrained friend will most certainly perish on the journey back to the king\'92s palace. I still have a ways to go yet, but if you insist on following me, please make sure you watch each other\'92s backs. This land and its inhabitants can be extremely treacherous. This place is nothing like the Other Side. I advise you all to tread carefully while you are here.\'94 He said, turning on his heel.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\ql\sl276\slmult1{\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\aspalpha\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\cf0\kerning0\hich\af2\langfe2052\dbch\af2\afs24\lang1081\loch\f3\fs22\lang4105\sl100\slmult0\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi720{\cf1\hich\af8\dbch\af8\rtlch \ltrch\loch\f6
\'93}{\cf1\hich\af8\dbch\af8\rtlch \ltrch\loch\fs24\loch\f6
OK! We pr\'96\'94 Marie started to speak, but stopped when Hortic turned around abruptly, and lifted his hand, palm out, towards her.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\ql\sl276\slmult1{\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\aspalpha\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\cf0\kerning0\hich\af2\langfe2052\dbch\af2\afs24\lang1081\loch\f3\fs22\lang4105\sl100\slmult0\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi720{\cf1\hich\af8\dbch\af8\rtlch \ltrch\loch\f6
