OK, it's not a good idea to venture out into the wilderness around here. I understand that.\'94 She put a hand on his shoulder to try to placate him. The motion assuaged his vexation on the outside, but I could tell he still harboured feelings of roiling apprehension. \'93That is why I suggested we go up to the Throne room and request His Highness to conjure up a lake which cannot be infested with such hazards. He could place it within the castle's grounds so it will be protected by the magickal barrier that surrounds us. Those two safeguards alone would make it easier to keep all those creatures out. As I mentioned a half hour ago, I studied a map of the grounds for hours yesterday, so I know for a fact that there is an empty plot of land south of the castle that would be perfect.\'94 Marie turned to look me straight in the eye.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\ql\sl276\slmult1{\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\aspalpha\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\cf0\kerning0\hich\af2\langfe2052\dbch\af2\afs24\lang1081\loch\f3\fs22\lang4105\sl100\slmult0\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi720{\cf1\hich\af8\dbch\af8\rtlch \ltrch\loch\f6
